1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,230
Search for a hotel near Amrita Hospital, and booking sites already have a page for it.

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:09,270
So the real question isn't whether options exist.

3
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,713
It's what families actually use — and what they still can't see.

4
00:00:13,363 --> 00:00:15,443
Right now, families piece it together.

5
00:00:15,493 --> 00:00:22,253
At Amrita, one family member can stay in the patient's room, and other relatives are pointed to a guest house on campus.

6
00:00:22,303 --> 00:00:25,283
Aster's international desk helps arrange hotels.

7
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:28,912
Everyone else turns to booking apps, private flats, or relatives.

8
00:00:29,562 --> 00:00:32,942
I mapped twelve providers around Aster Medcity and Amrita:

9
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:36,342
budget rooms, serviced apartments, guest houses, a Marriott.

10
00:00:36,392 --> 00:00:40,052
Some already market directly to patients and bystanders.

11
00:00:40,102 --> 00:00:42,576
So The Veedu wouldn't be starting in an empty market.

12
00:00:43,226 --> 00:00:44,596
Then I read the reviews.

13
00:00:44,646 --> 00:00:51,266
Twenty-five readable excerpts — well short of my target of a hundred, because most review pages weren't accessible.

14
00:00:51,316 --> 00:00:53,471
So this is a signal, not a statistic.

15
00:00:54,121 --> 00:00:56,131
Staff and cleanliness drew the most praise.

16
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:57,741
The complaints were practical:

17
00:00:57,791 --> 00:01:04,441
extra-person charges at checkout, broken AC and water supply, small rooms, no food on site.

18
00:01:04,491 --> 00:01:06,388
Safety never came up in this sample.

19
00:01:07,038 --> 00:01:10,928
Six reviews mentioned the hospital — and they were mostly about distance.

20
00:01:10,978 --> 00:01:15,418
At one guest house named after Amrita, a guest called it a twelve-minute walk.

21
00:01:15,468 --> 00:01:17,158
Another said it was a little away.

22
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:19,686
Location was its lowest-scored category.

23
00:01:20,386 --> 00:01:22,466
Plotting every option shows a pattern.

24
00:01:22,516 --> 00:01:25,586
General hotels have the most consistent information.

25
00:01:25,636 --> 00:01:29,095
The options built closest to medical needs often have the least.

26
00:01:29,745 --> 00:01:31,925
The segment worth investigating first:

27
00:01:31,975 --> 00:01:36,295
families from outside Kochi with a patient admitted for days or weeks.

28
00:01:36,345 --> 00:01:40,652
More people than the hospital room allows, staying longer than a typical guest.

29
00:01:41,302 --> 00:01:43,102
So here's the strongest insight.

30
00:01:43,152 --> 00:01:49,172
Distance is why these families choose a stay — and it's the fact listings state least consistently.

31
00:01:49,222 --> 00:01:50,682
The question for The Veedu:

32
00:01:50,732 --> 00:01:57,111
can it verify what caregivers decide on, well enough to be trusted over a listing that already says near Amrita?
